<Article h1={"Dead hang world record: the category decides the time"} subtitle={"The longest dead hang on the Guinness dead-hang-position page is 80 minutes 41 seconds, held by Kenta Adachi. Two other hanging titles list different times, including the women's record."} crumbs={[{"name":"Dead hang world record"}]} title="Dead Hang World Record: 80:41 and Every Hanging Record" description="Guinness lists three hanging records: the dead hang position, hanging from a bar, and a women's bar-hanging title. See each holder, time and date, checked 1 November 2026.">
<div class="article-body"><p class="small-copy">Updated November 1, 2026. Each Guinness listing below was opened and read on 1 November 2026. Guinness says records change on a daily basis and are not immediately published online.</p><h2 id="current-record">Longest dead hang: every Guinness hanging record</h2><p>Guinness lists three relevant hanging titles. "Dead hang position" (male) is 80 min 41 sec. "Hanging from a bar" is 4 hr 30 min 18 sec (male) and 53 min 51 sec (female). Differently named records are not interchangeable tests.</p><p>The public record pages do not state the competition rules. Check the current Guinness guidelines for the exact title before planning an official attempt.</p><p class="table-cue">Scroll horizontally on a smaller screen.</p><div class="table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Guinness hanging record categories"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Guinness category</th><th scope="col">Listed result</th><th scope="col">Holder</th><th scope="col">Achievement date</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Dead hang position (male)</th><td>80 min 41 sec</td><td>Kenta Adachi</td><td>18 November 2022</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Hanging from a bar (male)</th><td>4 hr 30 min 18 sec</td><td>Kenta Adachi</td><td>26 December 2025</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Hanging from a bar (female)</th><td>53 min 51 sec</td><td>Stefanie Millinger</td><td>11 July 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2 id="male-records">The two male listings</h2><p>Kenta Adachi's 2022 dead-hang-position result was achieved in Shunan, Japan. The separate bar-hanging result is dated December 2025 and was achieved in Yamaguchi, Japan. This page reports both as named by Guinness instead of declaring one an equivalent replacement for the other.</p><p>Check the official <a href="https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/118967-longest-duration-in-the-dead-hang-position">dead-hang-position listing</a> and <a href="https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/780102-longest-duration-hanging-from-a-bar-male">male bar-hanging listing</a>.</p><h2 id="female-records">Women's dead hang world record</h2><p>Guinness lists Stefanie Millinger's 53-minute 51-second bar hang in Salzburg, Austria. The achievement date is 11 July 2026. This is a different title from the male dead hang position record, and it should be named as the female hanging-from-a-bar title when quoting the result. The Guinness dead-hang-position listing is titled "(male)". I did not find a women's dead-hang-position listing on the Guinness pages I opened on 1 November 2026.</p><p>Read the official <a href="https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/785984-longest-duration-hanging-from-a-bar-female">female bar-hanging listing</a>.</p><h2 id="record-history">Why older articles show different times</h2><p>Guinness says records change daily and are not always published online immediately. An older result can remain online after another achievement or under a different title. Compare the exact category and achievement date before making a historical timeline. A search snippet alone is not enough to establish that two performances followed identical rules.</p><h2 id="how-they-train">Records do not provide a training prescription</h2><p>A record listing documents an achievement. It does not establish the holder's full training routine or a suitable routine for another person. Public Guinness summaries do not describe training or attempt methods.</p><h2 id="your-level">Compare your own sessions</h2><p>Your personal log does not need to resemble a world-record attempt. Record controlled holds with consistent equipment and assistance. We do not infer a population percentile from a record holder's time.</p><p>Use the <a href="/training-log/">timer and training log</a> for your own practice.</p><h2 id="faq">Is 80 minutes 41 seconds still listed?</h2><p>Yes. The public Guinness dead-hang-position listing showed that result when checked on 1 November 2026. The separate male bar-hanging page showed a longer result. Check the category and current official page when citing either.</p><h2>Get the planner or optional emails</h2><p>The blank training planner is free without signup. Email signup is optional and confirms registration rather than delivery of a particular message.</p><SignupForm client:load /></div>
</Article>
